<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::interceptor_stocks" target="israel_gaza_lebanon::civilian_casualty_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Accelerated consumption of interceptor missiles in the Russia–Ukraine war strains global production and shipment pipelines, delaying replenishment to Israeli air‑defense batteries and degrading interception rates, which raises civilian casualties during strikes and rocket/drone exchanges.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">israel_gaza_lebanon</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::interceptor_stocks" target="north_korea_threat::crossborder_incidents" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Heavy consumption of interceptor missiles and expendables in the Russia–Ukraine war depletes exportable inventories and delays deliveries to partners in East Asia, degrading allied air‑defence readiness and lowering the perceived cost for North Korea to carry out cross‑border strikes or airspace violations.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">north_korea_threat</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::interceptor_stocks" target="strait_hormuz_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Attrition of interceptor missile inventories in the Ukraine theater reduces the stocks available for transfer or redeployment to Gulf partners and naval task forces, lowering ship and port defensive capability and thereby increasing the rate of successful hostile incidents against vessels.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">strait_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::interceptor_stocks" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::critical_component_avail" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Large defense purchases and replenishment orders to replace spent interceptors consume production capacity and semiconductors/advanced electronics, crowding out civilian supply chains and reducing the immediate availability of critical components for advanced commercial tech suppliers, including those serving Chinese firms.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
