<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::airspace_safety_risk" target="israel_gaza_lebanon::great_power_engagement" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in systemic airspace safety incidents tied to the Russia–Ukraine conflict forces major powers to reallocate military assets, intelligence and diplomatic bandwidth to European air defense and escalation management, lowering the depth and immediacy of their engagement in the Israel–Gaza–Lebanon crisis.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">israel_gaza_lebanon</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::airspace_safety_risk" target="north_korea_threat::regional_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in high‑visibility airspace safety incidents linked to the Ukraine conflict prompts faster multilateral civil‑military coordination and information‑sharing norms among concerned states, which regional actors in Northeast Asia adopt to mitigate similar risks, thereby increasing alliance coordination and cohesion.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">north_korea_threat</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::airspace_safety_risk" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_uncertainty" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising incidents and near‑misses in civilian airspace spur immediate regulators to propose emergency rules on drone operations, spectrum use, and cross‑border data/asset controls, increasing short‑term uncertainty among technology firms and investors about upcoming regulatory constraints affecting US–China tech interactions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
