  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A sudden drop in availability of critical components (motors, cameras, GNSS modules, spare electronics) used in commercial drones and guidance kits—driven by export restrictions or supply-chain disruption from the US‑China tech rivalry—directly degrades militant UAV/precision-weapon readiness and maintenance, reducing the frequency and reach of cross‑border strikes.</data>
